&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Company Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are Olsson. We engineer and design solutions that improve the world around us. As a company, we promise to always be responsive, transparent, and focused on results – for our people, our clients, and our company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a people-centric firm, so it’s no surprise our greatest asset is our people. The impact this creates is an environment that encourages our people to grow and be creative with their talents. This approach builds a culture that is uniquely Olsson. It allows us to grow our people as we grow our business. This, in turn, creates a lasting impact on the world around us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Associate Electrical Engineer to join our Federal Engineering and Design Team. In this role, you will support the planning and design of electrical systems for federal facilities and infrastructure projects. Working alongside experienced engineers and designers, you will gain exposure to federal design standards, including UFC, DoD, and VA requirements, while developing technical expertise in power distribution, lighting, communications, and other building electrical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position provides hands-on experience designing mission-critical facilities and offers the opportunity to contribute to projects that support national interests while building a strong foundation for your engineering career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the design of electrical systems for federal facilities, including power distribution, lighting, grounding, communications, and life safety systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform engineering calculations, system layouts, and equipment selections under the guidance of licensed engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and apply knowledge of electrical engineering principles, codes, standards, and industry best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize engineering and design software such as Revit, AutoCAD, or other electrical modeling and analysis tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with project schedules, design coordination efforts, and interdisciplinary collaboration with mechanical, civil, structural, and architectural teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research applicable federal design criteria and recommend solutions to technical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain experience creating and maintaining project information within the firm&#39;s project management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May travel to project sites and federal installations to support design development, construction, and project coordination activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
