&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working collaboratively with others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Having ownership in the work you do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using your talents to positively affect communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You bring to the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to contribute and work well on a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-4 years of engineering experience.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dec 2026 or May 2027 graduates encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must obtain or have an Engineer Intern (EI) certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AutoCAD (or similar software).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
